comment 1617 "{\n  \"body\": \"PR stuck: a finished check that did not pass holds this PR `unstable` (`11111111`).\\n\\nGitHub reports this PR `unstable`, and every check run on this head has finished.\\nThe one(s) that did not pass:\\n\\n* `report` — **cancelled**\\n\\nThe gate may well be green (on this head it reads **success**) and this PR still\\ncannot merge: `.github/steward/merge-ready.sh` merges only what GitHub calls `clean`,\\ndeliberately, and `unstable` is not `clean`. Nothing in this repository re-runs a\\ncheck that has completed, and the lap pushes only when `dev` has moved — so this\\nstays exactly as it is until somebody acts. #1617 sat like this on 2026-09-21 with\\na green gate and a `report` check cancelled by the next push's sweep.\\n\\nWhat clears it: **re-run the check that did not pass.**\\n\\n```\\ngh api -X POST repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/actions/runs/37095687592/rerun\\n```\\n\\nor press **Re-run** on it from the Checks tab. It went `clean` within a minute of\\nthat on #1617. Do NOT push an empty commit to kick CI: that is refused everywhere\\nelse in this repository, and it would re-gate a tree the gate has already passed.\\n\\nIf it is waiting on the OWNER on purpose, park it with `hold` — this reporter\\nreads labels first and leaves a held PR alone. If it is merely UNFINISHED, hand\\nit to the next run instead:\\n\\n    .github/steward/pr-rest.sh resume 1617 --why \\\"...\\\" --waits-on nothing\\n\\nwhich writes the reason where a machine and a person can both read it.\\n\\n---\\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\\n\"\n}\n"
